WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.280
This is very, very interesting. President&nbsp;
Joe Biden is currently experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:15.520
the highest initial approval rating of any&nbsp;
president dating back 28 years to Bill Clinton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:26.320
in 1993. The All America Economic Survey has found&nbsp;
that Joe Biden has a 62 percent approval rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:34.160
right now. His initial approval rating that beats&nbsp;
the first presidential rating of Barack Obama, of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.800
George W. Bush, of Bill Clinton, and, of course,&nbsp;
of Donald Trump. And in fact, Joe Biden's initial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.680
rating of 62 percent approval is 18 points higher&nbsp;
than that of Donald Trump. There are a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:56.240
of takeaways here. First of all, when we look at&nbsp;
these numbers and understand that there are hyper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:02.320
partizan enclaves of Americans that will either&nbsp;
always approve or always disapprove of a president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.800
merely based on political party, you realize&nbsp;
that the real range, it's not really zero to 100,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.800
it's probably more like, I don't know, 20 to 80&nbsp;
or twenty five to seventy five or whatever. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.200
when you see a rating of 36, that is much&nbsp;
closer to the bottom than it would seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.720
because some portion will always approve of&nbsp;
the president. When you see a number like 62,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.560
that's much closer to the top because because some&nbsp;
portion will always disapprove. So, number one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.120
the difference between 62 and 36 is much&nbsp;
bigger than merely the difference between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.280
the two numbers. When you understand American&nbsp;
politics, that's number one. Number two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:46.560
important takeaway is that this really reinforces&nbsp;
that Donald Trump could have easily won reelection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.800
if back in March he had simply said this&nbsp;
is serious, the doctors know what to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:59.360
Let's do what they say. Oh, they say wear masks.&nbsp;
We are printing American flag masks, do the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:06.320
patriotic thing. If Trump and his staffers were&nbsp;
regularly pictured from the beginning with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.600
patriotic American flag masks, I know that might&nbsp;
violate flag code. OK, don't email me about that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.840
Donald Trump would have sailed to reelection,&nbsp;
as we saw so many world leaders do, who dealt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:25.040
with the virus. Well, and that is confirmed by&nbsp;
this polling. Much of Joe Biden's early approval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.760
is based on his handling of the coronavirus on&nbsp;
which he has a nearly 70 percent approval rating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.800
So Trump could be president right now, and it's&nbsp;
because of Trump that he is not. We'll continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.960
to follow Joe Biden's approval. It could go up.&nbsp;
It could go down. I really don't know. These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.720
unique circumstances in which we find ourselves.&nbsp;
But I want to hear from you. Where do you believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:51.760
Joe Biden's approval will go and or does it depend&nbsp;
on accomplishing something like, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.120
getting the covid relief checks to Americans?
I believe if he fails to do it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.440
it will be a political disaster, but I do&nbsp;
believe he is going to do it. Let me know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:59.677
your thoughts. I'm on Twitter at David Pakman,&nbsp;
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman dot com.

